threads.body:
`generation.getOutput().getText()` is nullable in Spring AI (an `AssistantMessage` carrying only tool calls has null text), and `Value.of((String) null)` throws `NullPointerException`. Because the loop body sits inside `catch (Throwable ignored)`, the first null-content choice aborts the loop, so that choice and every later one silently lose their `gen_ai.choice` event. The streaming aggregation and the span attribute serializer in this PR both already null-check this same value. `emitPromptEvents` has the same problem for assistant messages in the prompt history.

```suggestion
          if (content != null) {
            message.put("content", Value.of(content));
          }
```

