threads.body:
Jackson Core ships `JsonStringEncoder` for exactly this, and Spring AI 1.x already puts `jackson-databind` on the compile classpath. Other modules delegate JSON encoding to the instrumented library's own serializer the same way: AWS uses `SdkJsonGenerator`, Mongo uses `JsonWriter`, and OpenSearch uses Jackson. Muzzle will verify the API across the supported Spring AI range.

```suggestion
  private static void appendJsonString(StringBuilder result, @Nullable String value) {
    result.append('"');
    JsonStringEncoder.getInstance().quoteAsString(value == null ? "" : value, result);
    result.append('"');
  }
```

Needs `import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.io.JsonStringEncoder;`.

